
  # String / Date functions

   Query and what it does :-

   String concatenation -> CONCAT(first_name, ' ', last_name)

   Slice a string -> SUBSTRING(email, 1, 5)

   Case conversion -> UPPER(name) / LOWER(name)

   Strip whitespace -> TRIM (name)

   Current date-time -> NOW() / CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

   Extract just the date part -> DATE(created_at)

   Difference between dates -> DATEDIFF(NOW(), created_at) (MySQL) / NOW() - created_at (Postgres)

   Add/subtract time -> DATE_ADD(created_at, INTERVAL 7 DAY)

   Return first non-null value — handy default-value pattern -> COALESCE(discount, 0)

   Conditional logic inline in a SELECT ->  CASE WHEN amount > 1000 THEN 'HIGH' WHEN amount >
                                            100 THEN 'MEDIUM' ELSE 'LOW' END AS tier

